  <dmn:decision id="_DE2C84D6-294A-453B-94F7-FE5A6DAE6E50" name="checks">
    <dmn:description>Requires Philadelphia residence, a PWD residential account with the bill in the applicant name, age at least 65 on asOfDate (today when omitted), and prepared phl-senior-water income at/below $42,100. The inclusive comparison follows rates effective 2026-09-01 §5.2(b), rather than the summary page wording. Prepare income for the senior program; do not automatically apply TAP exclusions. The rate document describes a 25% discount, but the model returns eligibility rather than a calculated bill. The next rates document must be reviewed before changing the fixed ceiling. One City water-assistance application selects a program; TAP and the senior discount need not stack. Household screening only: application windows, available funds, waitlists and provider scheduling do not change checks/isEligible. No award, account establishment or work approval is calculated. Policy review preserved from 2026-10-15. Named entries invoke reusable check Decision Services; inspect those models for their policy interpretation and input contract.</dmn:description>
    <dmn:extensionElements>
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia water assistance — program comparison" url="https://cap.phila.gov/eligibility/" />
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia water assistance — application and hardship guidance" url="https://www.phila.gov/services/payments-assistance-taxes/payment-plans-and-assistance-programs/senior-citizen-programs/apply-for-water-bill-customer-assistance/" />
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia water rates effective 2026-09-01 — §5.2(b), senior discount" url="https://water.phila.gov/wp-content/uploads/files/rates-and-charges-2026-09-01.pdf" />
